  "term": "SBS",
  "definition": "SBS stands for stimulated Brillouin scattering, an optical effect used in devices such as filters, sensing systems, and spectrum analysis. In this packet, it refers to a light-based process in fiber systems whose performance can be affected by polarization changes unless compensated.",
